    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d401">

                <pb facs="0522" n="437" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg437"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3207</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of the Third Assistant Secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-22"><hi rendition="#italic">August 22,
                        1919</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Debuchi told me today that a report was coming to him by mail in the Tientsin
                    matter, and that his Consul General could not agree with the American Consul
                    General, and that there appeared <pb facs="0523" n="438" xml:id="pg438"/> to be
                    a deadlock. He said that his Government wanted to make some disposition of
                    it.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Breckinridge Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
